# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `service-typescript` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's TypeScript service conventions (platform ADR-124):

- Node {{ node_major }} LTS and pnpm via devbox; ESM, TypeScript strict, compiled with `tsc` to `dist/`
- Fastify 5, pino JSON logging{% if needs_observability %}, prom-client metrics on `/metrics`, OpenTelemetry tracing (OTLP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set){% endif %}
{%- if needs_database %}
- PostgreSQL through Drizzle ORM; SQL migrations in `drizzle/` (drizzle-kit), applied at startup; Testcontainers tests
{%- endif %}
- ESLint (typescript-eslint) + `tsc --noEmit` as the quality gate; `pnpm audit` for dependencies
- Vitest with an 80 % coverage gate; smoke tests named `@smoke` in `tests/smoke/`
- Distroless Node image, numeric non-root user → `{{ docker_registry }}/{{ project_name }}`
- No Kubernetes manifests here: the system's gitops-app repo owns them (platform ADR-017); this repo ships a container image
- GitHub topic `deployable-service` for ArgoCD discovery
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-ts` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, Dockerfile, Node bump, lint and test config) arrive through `copier update`; `src/`, `tests/`, `drizzle/`, `package.json` and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
